{"id":"mahabharata-3-271","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":271,"title":"एकसप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 271 · Kumbhakarna slain","summary":{"en":"Kumbhakarna storms out, devouring monkeys, and seizes Sugriva. Lakshmana attacks him, cuts off his upraised arms with razor-edged arrows, and slays him with the Brahma weapon, while monkeys and Rakshasas slaughter each other by the hundred.","kn":"ಕುಂಭಕರ್ಣನು ಕಪಿಗಳನ್ನು ನುಂಗುತ್ತಾ ನುಗ್ಗಿ ಸುಗ್ರೀವನನ್ನು ಹಿಡಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಲಕ್ಷ್ಮಣನು ಅವನ ಮೇಲೆರಗಿ ಎತ್ತಿದ ತೋಳುಗಳನ್ನು ಕ್ಷುರಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮಾಸ್ತ್ರದಿಂದ ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕಪಿಗಳು ರಾಕ್ಷಸರು ನೂರಾರು ಸಂಖ್ಯೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"कुम्भकर्ण वानरों को निगलता हुआ निकलता है और सुग्रीव को पकड़ लेता है। लक्ष्मण उस पर आक्रमण कर उसकी उठी भुजाएँ छुरे जैसे बाणों से काट देते हैं और ब्रह्मास्त्र से उसे मार डालते हैं, जबकि वानर और राक्षस सैकड़ों की संख्या में एक-दूसरे को मारते हैं।","te":"కుంభకర్ణుడు వానరులను మింగుతూ దూసుకువచ్చి సుగ్రీవుని పట్టుకుంటాడు. లక్ష్మణుడు అతనిపై దాడి చేసి ఎత్తిన చేతులను క్షురబాణాలతో నరికి బ్రహ్మాస్త్రంతో సంహరిస్తాడు; వానరులు, రాక్షసులు వందల సంఖ్యలో ఒకరినొకరు చంపుకుంటారు.","ta":"கும்பகர்ணன் வானரங்களை விழுங்கியபடி பாய்ந்து ஸுக்ரீவனைப் பற்றுகிறான். லக்ஷ்மணன் அவனைத் தாக்கி உயர்த்திய கைகளைக் கத்தி போன்ற அம்புகளால் வெட்டி ப்ரஹ்மாஸ்திரத்தால் கொல்ல, வானரங்களும் அரக்கர்களும் நூற்றுக்கணக்கில் ஒருவரையொருவர் கொல்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"കുംഭകർണ്ണൻ കുരങ്ങന്മാരെ തിന്നുകൊണ്ട് പുറത്തുവന്ന് സുഗ്രീവനെ പിടികൂടുന്നു. ലക്ഷ്മണൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു, മൂർച്ചയുള്ള അമ്പുകൾകൊണ്ട് ഉയർത്തിയ കൈകൾ അറുക്കുന്നു, പിന്നെ ബ്രഹ്മാസ്ത്രംകൊണ്ട് വധിക്കുന്നു; അതിനിടെ കുരങ്ങന്മാരും രാക്ഷസന്മാരും നൂറുകണക്കിന് പേരായി പരസ്പരം കൊല്ലുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.271; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो विनिर्याय पुरात्कुम्भकर्णः सहानुगः ।\nअपश्यत्कपिसैन्यं तज्जितकाश्यग्रतः स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kumbhakarna left the city with his followers and saw the monkey army standing, with Hanuman's side in front."}},{"n":2,"text":"तमभ्येत्याशु हरयः परिवार्य समन्ततः ।\nअभ्यघ्नंश्च महाकायैर्बहुभिर्जगतीरुहैः ।\nकरजैरतुदंश्चान्ये विहाय भयमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Monkeys quickly came up and surrounded him on all sides, striking him with many huge trees; others, putting aside great fear, tore him with their nails."}},{"n":3,"text":"बहुधा युध्यमानास्ते युद्धमार्गैः प्लवंगमाः ।\nनानाप्रहरणैर्भीमं राक्षसेन्द्रमताडयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fighting in many ways according to the rules of war, the monkeys beat the terrible lord of rakshasas with all kinds of weapons."}},{"n":4,"text":"स ताड्यमानः प्रहसन्भक्षयामास वानरान् ।\nपनसं च गवाक्षं च वज्रबाहुं च वानरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beaten, he laughed and devoured monkeys, among them Panasa, Gavaksha, and the monkey Vajrabahu."}},{"n":5,"text":"तद्दृष्ट्वा व्यथनं कर्म कुम्भकर्णस्य रक्षसः ।\nउदक्रोशन्परित्रस्तास्तारप्रभृतयस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the rakshasa Kumbhakarna's painful work, Tara and the others cried out in fear."}},{"n":6,"text":"तं तारमुच्चैः क्रोशन्तमन्यांश्च हरियूथपान् ।\nअभिदुद्राव सुग्रीवः कुम्भकर्णमपेतभीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sugriva, without fear, ran at Kumbhakarna while Tara and the other monkey leaders cried out loudly."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततोऽभिपत्य वेगेन कुम्भकर्णं महामनाः ।\nशालेन जघ्निवान्मूर्ध्नि बलेन कपिकुञ्जरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great-minded bull among monkeys, rushing at him with speed, struck Kumbhakarna on the head with a sala tree, with all his strength."}},{"n":8,"text":"स महात्मा महावेगः कुम्भकर्णस्य मूर्धनि ।\nबिभेद शालं सुग्रीवो न चैवाव्यथयत्कपिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great-souled, swift Sugriva shattered the tree on Kumbhakarna's head, but did not distress him."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो विनद्य प्रहसञ्शालस्पर्शविबोधितः ।\nदोर्भ्यामादाय सुग्रीवं कुम्भकर्णोऽहरद्बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, awakened by the touch of the sala tree, Kumbhakarna roared and laughed, seized Sugriva in both arms, and carried him off by force."}},{"n":10,"text":"ह्रियमाणं तु सुग्रीवं कुम्भकर्णेन रक्षसा ।\nअवेक्ष्याभ्यद्रवद्वीरः सौमित्रिर्मित्रनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Sugriva carried off by the rakshasa Kumbhakarna, Lakshmana, son of Sumitra and delight of his friends, ran after him."}},{"n":11,"text":"सोऽभिपत्य महावेगं रुक्मपुङ्खं महाशरम् ।\nप्राहिणोत्कुम्भकर्णाय लक्ष्मणः परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rushing forward, Lakshmana, killer of enemy heroes, sent a great arrow of great speed with a golden shaft at Kumbhakarna."}},{"n":12,"text":"स तस्य देहावरणं भित्त्वा देहं च सायकः ।\nजगाम दारयन्भूमिं रुधिरेण समुक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That arrow pierced his armor and his body, and tore into the earth, drenched with blood."}},{"n":13,"text":"तथा स भिन्नहृदयः समुत्सृज्य कपीश्वरम् ।\nकुम्भकर्णो महेष्वासः प्रगृहीतशिलायुधः ।\nअभिदुद्राव सौमित्रिमुद्यम्य महतीं शिलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his heart pierced, the great archer Kumbhakarna let go of the monkey king, took up a rock as a weapon, lifted the huge stone, and ran at Lakshmana."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्याभिद्रवतस्तूर्णं क्षुराभ्यामुच्छ्रितौ करौ ।\nचिच्छेद निशिताग्राभ्यां स बभूव चतुर्भुजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he charged, Lakshmana quickly cut off his raised arms with two razor-edged arrows, and Kumbhakarna became four-armed."}},{"n":15,"text":"तानप्यस्य भुजान्सर्वान्प्रगृहीतशिलायुधान् ।\nक्षुरैश्चिच्छेद लघ्वस्त्रं सौमित्रिः प्रतिदर्शयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showing his light skill in weapons, Lakshmana cut off all those arms too, gripping their rock weapons, with razor arrows."}},{"n":16,"text":"स बभूवातिकायश्च बहुपादशिरोभुजः ।\nतं ब्रह्मास्त्रेण सौमित्रिर्ददाहाद्रिचयोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He then became huge, with many feet, heads, and arms, and Lakshmana burned him, who looked like a heap of mountains, with the Brahma weapon."}},{"n":17,"text":"स पपात महावीर्यो दिव्यास्त्राभिहतो रणे ।\nमहाशनिविनिर्दग्धः पादपोऽङ्कुरवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"That mighty one fell in battle, struck down by the divine weapon, like a sprouting tree burned by a great thunderbolt."}},{"n":18,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा वृत्रसंकाशं कुम्भकर्णं तरस्विनम् ।\nगतासुं पतितं भूमौ राक्षसाः प्राद्रवन्भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the mighty Kumbhakarna, who looked like Vritra, lying lifeless on the ground, the rakshasas fled in fear."}},{"n":19,"text":"तथा तान्द्रवतो योधान्दृष्ट्वा तौ दूषणानुजौ ।\nअवस्थाप्याथ सौमित्रिं संक्रुद्धावभ्यधावताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those warriors fleeing, Dushana's two younger brothers halted them, and, enraged, ran at Lakshmana."}},{"n":20,"text":"तावाद्रवन्तौ संक्रुद्धौ वज्रवेगप्रमाथिनौ ।\nप्रतिजग्राह सौमित्रिर्विनद्योभौ पतत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Vajravega and Pramathin charged in rage, Lakshmana roared and met both with his arrows."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः सुतुमुलं युद्धमभवल्लोमहर्षणम् ।\nदूषणानुजयोः पार्थ लक्ष्मणस्य च धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a tremendous, hair-raising battle took place, son of Pritha, between Dushana's younger brothers and the wise Lakshmana."}},{"n":22,"text":"महता शरवर्षेण राक्षसौ सोऽभ्यवर्षत ।\nतौ चापि वीरौ संक्रुद्धावुभौ तौ समवर्षताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lakshmana rained a great shower of arrows on the two rakshasas, and those two enraged heroes rained arrows back at him."}},{"n":23,"text":"मुहूर्तमेवमभवद्वज्रवेगप्रमाथिनोः ।\nसौमित्रेश्च महाबाहोः संप्रहारः सुदारुणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a time there was a dreadful clash between Vajravega and Pramathin and the mighty-armed son of Sumitra."}},{"n":24,"text":"अथाद्रिशृङ्गमादाय हनूमान्मारुतात्मजः ।\nअभिद्रुत्याददे प्राणान्वज्रवेगस्य रक्षसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Hanuman, the son of the wind, took a mountain peak, rushed forward, and took the life of the rakshasa Vajravega."}},{"n":25,"text":"नीलश्च महता ग्राव्णा दूषणावरजं हरिः ।\nप्रमाथिनमभिद्रुत्य प्रममाथ महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nila the monkey, very strong, rushed at Dushana's other younger brother Pramathin with a huge stone and crushed him."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः प्रावर्तत पुनः संग्रामः कटुकोदयः ।\nरामरावणसैन्यानामन्योन्यमभिधावताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the battle began again, with bitter outcome, as the armies of Rama and Ravana ran against one another."}},{"n":27,"text":"शतशो नैरृतान्वन्या जघ्नुर्वन्यांश्च नैरृताः ।\nनैरृतास्तत्र वध्यन्ते प्रायशो न तु वानराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Forest dwellers killed rakshasas by hundreds and rakshasas killed forest dwellers, but mostly rakshasas were slain there, not monkeys."}}]}]}